('127.255.d.5.A',4,'A bank''s security camera and alarm systems are examples of:','["Marketing", "Loan products", "Loss prevention measures", "Taxes"]'::jsonb,2,'They deter and detect crime.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.B',3,'Banks keep reserve accounts at the:','["County clerk", "School district", "Post office", "Federal Reserve"]'::jsonb,3,'Reserves are held with the Fed.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.B',4,'The Federal Reserve also provides banks with services such as:','["Check clearing and cash supply", "Insurance", "Free loans for all", "Stock tips"]'::jsonb,0,'The Fed supports payments.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.C',3,'A teller receiving a torn or damaged bill should:','["Keep it", "Follow the bank''s procedure for damaged currency", "Tape it and re-circulate", "Throw it away"]'::jsonb,1,'Damaged currency is processed by procedure.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.C',4,'When the cash drawer is $5 over at the end of the day, a teller should:','["Take the $5", "Hide it", "Report and document the difference", "Ignore it"]'::jsonb,2,'Overages must be reported.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.D',3,'The three Cs of credit are character, capacity, and:','["Color", "Contest", "Cash", "Collateral"]'::jsonb,3,'Collateral secures a loan.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.D',4,'A loan applicant with high income but huge existing debt may be turned down because of poor:','["Capacity to repay", "Address style", "Phone brand", "Hair length"]'::jsonb,0,'Capacity measures ability to repay.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.E',3,'A borrower falls 60 days behind on a loan. The bank''s first step is usually to:','["Cancel the account without notice", "Contact the borrower and discuss options", "Ignore it", "Sell the home immediately"]'::jsonb,1,'Workouts come first.','original'),
('127.255.d.5.E',4,'Restructuring a troubled loan by changing its terms is called a:','["Closing", "Foreclosure", "Workout or modification", "Audit"]'::jsonb,2,'Workouts avoid defaults.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.A',3,'A bank compliance program should include policies, training, monitoring, and:','["Parties", "Giveaways", "Slogans", "Audits and corrective action"]'::jsonb,3,'Programs need testing.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.A',4,'The main goal of a compliance program is to:','["Ensure the bank follows laws and regulations", "Cut staff", "Avoid customers", "Increase fees"]'::jsonb,0,'Compliance prevents violations.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.B',3,'A compliance audit reviews whether a bank:','["Has nice furniture", "Follows laws and its own procedures", "Advertises well", "Has many branches"]'::jsonb,1,'Audits test adherence.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.B',4,'Findings from a compliance audit are usually reported to:','["The press", "Customers only", "Management and the board", "Competitors"]'::jsonb,2,'Governance requires reporting.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.C',3,'If a compliance plan lacks employee training, the plan is:','["Optional", "Illegal to read", "Perfect", "Incomplete"]'::jsonb,3,'Training is a key element.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.C',4,'An effective compliance plan assigns:','["Clear responsibility for each requirement", "No one", "Only customers", "Everyone vaguely"]'::jsonb,0,'Accountability matters.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.D',3,'The Truth in Lending Act requires lenders to disclose:','["Employee salaries", "The cost of credit including APR", "Stock prices", "Branch addresses"]'::jsonb,1,'TILA mandates disclosure.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.D',4,'The Equal Credit Opportunity Act prohibits lenders from denying credit because of:','["Income", "Credit score", "Race, sex, or marital status", "Debts"]'::jsonb,2,'ECOA bans discrimination.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.E',3,'E-compliance in banking includes protecting customers'' data in:','["Window displays", "Paper maps", "Parking", "Online and mobile banking"]'::jsonb,3,'E-compliance covers digital channels.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.E',4,'A bank sending unencrypted customer data over email risks violating:','["Privacy and data security rules", "Zoning law", "Labor holidays", "Traffic law"]'::jsonb,0,'Data must be protected.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.F',3,'The Office of the Comptroller of the Currency supervises:','["School districts", "National banks", "Insurance firms", "Credit unions"]'::jsonb,1,'The OCC charters and supervises national banks.','original'),
('127.255.d.6.F',4,'The National Credit Union Administration regulates:','["Commercial banks", "Stock exchanges", "Federal credit unions", "Pawn shops"]'::jsonb,2,'NCUA oversees credit unions.','original'),
('127.255.d.7.A',3,'A friendly greeting and remembering a customer''s name help to:','["Raise fees", "Slow lines", "Annoy customers", "Build positive relationships and loyalty"]'::jsonb,3,'Relationships bring repeat business.','original'),
('127.255.d.7.A',4,'A banker who follows up after a loan closing is:','["Cultivating a long-term customer relationship", "Breaking the law", "Wasting time", "Ending service"]'::jsonb,0,'Follow-up builds trust.','original'),
('127.255.d.7.B',3,'To exceed expectations, a banker might:','["Delay the answer", "Solve the problem before the customer has to ask", "Ignore the request", "Shorten hours"]'::jsonb,1,'Proactive service delights.','original'),
('127.255.d.7.B',4,'A customer is told a loan decision takes 5 days but receives it in 2. This:','["Is irrelevant", "Meets expectations exactly", "Exceeds expectations", "Fails expectations"]'::jsonb,2,'Faster than promised exceeds expectations.','original'),
('127.255.d.7.C',3,'Banks work with accountants and attorneys because they:','["Hide customers", "Never speak", "Compete on every account", "Refer clients to one another and share expertise"]'::jsonb,3,'Professionals form referral networks.','original'),
('127.255.d.7.C',4,'A bank and a real estate agent can both benefit by:','["Referring clients to each other", "Ignoring each other", "Avoiding competition", "Closing accounts"]'::jsonb,0,'Referrals expand business.','original'),
('127.255.d.8.A',3,'A bank earns most of its profit from the difference between the interest it earns on loans and the interest it:','["Owes in taxes", "Pays on deposits", "Pays in rent", "Charges for pens"]'::jsonb,1,'This is the net interest margin.','original'),
('127.255.d.8.A',4,'A bank earns 6% on loans and pays 2% on deposits. The interest spread is:','["8%", "2%", "4%", "12%"]'::jsonb,2,'6 - 2 = 4.','original'),
('127.255.d.8.B',3,'A bank has $50 million in assets and earns $500,000 in net income. Its return on assets is:','["10%", "5%", "0.1%", "1%"]'::jsonb,3,'500,000 / 50,000,000 = 0.01.','original'),
('127.255.d.8.B',4,'Compound interest on $2,000 at 3% for 2 years is about:','["$121.80", "$180", "$60", "$120"]'::jsonb,0,'2,000 x 1.0609 = 2,121.80.','original'),
('127.256.d.5',3,'A merchandising business earns income mainly by:','["Providing only services", "Buying goods and reselling them", "Printing money", "Lending funds"]'::jsonb,1,'Merchandisers resell inventory.','original'),
('127.256.d.5',4,'A store buys goods costing $60,000 and sells them for $90,000. Gross profit is:','["$150,000", "$60,000", "$30,000", "$90,000"]'::jsonb,2,'90,000 - 60,000 = 30,000.','original'),
('127.256.d.1.A',3,'The main purpose of accounting is to:','["Sell goods", "Design logos", "Hire workers", "Record and report financial information for decision makers"]'::jsonb,3,'Accounting provides financial information.','original'),
('127.256.d.1.A',4,'Financial reports such as the balance sheet are mainly used by owners, lenders, and:','["Investors", "Strangers", "Competitors'' pets", "Weather analysts"]'::jsonb,0,'Stakeholders use reports.','original'),
('127.256.d.1.B',3,'Accurate accounting helps industry by:','["Raising prices", "Giving investors reliable information", "Hiding losses", "Delaying taxes"]'::jsonb,1,'Trust requires accuracy.','original'),
('127.256.d.1.B',4,'Lenders review a company''s financial statements before approving a loan to judge its:','["Employee hobbies", "Logo design", "Ability to repay", "Office decor"]'::jsonb,2,'Statements show repayment ability.','original'),
('127.256.d.1.C',3,'GAAP stands for:','["General Asset And Profit", "Government Accounting And Payroll", "Great Accounting And Planning", "Generally Accepted Accounting Principles"]'::jsonb,3,'GAAP sets reporting standards.','original'),
('127.256.d.1.C',4,'GAAP is used so that financial statements are:','["Consistent and comparable across companies", "Ignored", "Secret", "Random"]'::jsonb,0,'Standards promote comparability.','original'),
('127.256.d.2.A',3,'An accountant who keeps client information private is practicing:','["Gossip", "Confidentiality", "Fraud", "Negligence"]'::jsonb,1,'Confidentiality is an ethical duty.','original'),
('127.256.d.2.A',4,'An accountant who is pressured to hide a loss from auditors should:','["Quit silently", "Hide it", "Refuse and follow ethical standards", "Delete records"]'::jsonb,2,'Integrity comes first.','original'),
('127.256.d.2.B',3,'Entry-level accounting jobs often require at least:','["No schooling", "A law degree", "A medical degree", "An associate or bachelor''s degree"]'::jsonb,3,'Education varies.','original'),
('127.256.d.2.B',4,'A bookkeeper''s primary role is to:','["Record daily financial transactions", "Design software", "Audit public companies", "Set tax law"]'::jsonb,0,'Bookkeepers record transactions.','original'),
('127.256.d.2.C',3,'The credential most associated with licensed public accountants is the:','["CEO", "CPA", "CFA", "CNA"]'::jsonb,1,'CPA is Certified Public Accountant.','original'),
('127.256.d.2.C',4,'A CPA candidate must pass the:','["Bar exam", "SAT", "Uniform CPA Examination", "Driver''s test"]'::jsonb,2,'The exam is required for licensure.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.A',3,'Which step comes first in the accounting cycle?','["Close the books", "Post-closing trial balance", "Prepare financial statements", "Analyze source documents and transactions"]'::jsonb,3,'The cycle begins with analysis of transactions.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.A',4,'The final step of the accounting cycle is preparing a:','["Post-closing trial balance", "Check", "Invoice", "Source document"]'::jsonb,0,'It verifies balances after closing.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.B',3,'The accounting equation is:','["Equity = Debts", "Assets = Liabilities + Owner''s Equity", "Assets = Revenue - Expenses", "Liabilities = Assets + Equity"]'::jsonb,1,'Basic equation.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.B',4,'A business buys $500 of supplies with cash. Total assets:','["Fall $500", "Double", "Stay the same", "Rise $500"]'::jsonb,2,'One asset replaces another.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.C',3,'A chart of accounts is a list of:','["Employees", "Suppliers'' logos", "Customers'' birthdays", "All accounts a business uses"]'::jsonb,3,'It organizes accounts.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.C',4,'In a typical numbering scheme, asset accounts usually begin with:','["1", "5", "9", "4"]'::jsonb,0,'Assets start at 1.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.D',3,'A general journal entry records the date, accounts, and:','["Slogans", "Debit and credit amounts", "Employee names", "The weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Entries need amounts.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.D',4,'When a business pays $200 cash for rent, which entry is correct?','["Credit Rent Expense only", "Debit Cash, credit Rent Expense", "Debit Rent Expense, credit Cash", "Debit Rent Expense, credit Revenue"]'::jsonb,2,'Expense up, cash down.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.E',3,'Posting means transferring journal entries to the:','["Bank statement", "Invoice", "Check stub", "General ledger accounts"]'::jsonb,3,'Posting updates ledgers.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.E',4,'After posting, a ledger account shows its running:','["Balance", "Slogan", "Mascot", "Address"]'::jsonb,0,'Balance updates after each entry.','original')
