('127.256.d.3.J',3,'An income statement reports:','["Assets only", "Revenue and expenses for a period", "Cash on hand at one date", "Liabilities only"]'::jsonb,1,'It shows performance over time.','original'),
('127.256.d.3.J',4,'Revenue of $80,000 and expenses of $62,000 result in:','["Net loss of $18,000", "Net income of $142,000", "Net income of $18,000", "Net income of $80,000"]'::jsonb,2,'80,000 - 62,000 = 18,000.','original'),
('127.256.d.4.A',3,'Requiring one employee to open the mail and another to record payments is an example of:','["Waste", "Bias", "Delay", "Internal control"]'::jsonb,3,'Segregation of duties prevents theft.','original'),
('127.256.d.4.A',4,'Limiting access to the company checkbook to authorized people is a:','["Cash control procedure", "Pricing step", "Marketing step", "Hiring step"]'::jsonb,0,'Controls protect cash.','original'),
