('127.256.d.4.D',3,'A bank service charge on the statement is recorded as:','["Revenue", "A bank service expense", "A loan", "Owner''s investment"]'::jsonb,1,'Fees are expenses.','original'),
('127.256.d.4.D',4,'A note collected by the bank for the business increases the:','["Payroll", "Bank fee", "Checkbook balance", "Rent"]'::jsonb,2,'Collections add to the book balance.','original'),
('127.256.d.4.E',3,'Electronic funds transfer benefits a business by:','["Using more paper", "Slowing deposits", "Hiding transactions", "Moving money faster with fewer errors"]'::jsonb,3,'EFT is quick and accurate.','original'),
('127.256.d.4.E',4,'Direct deposit of payroll is an example of:','["Electronic funds transfer", "Petty cash", "Trial balance", "Closing entry"]'::jsonb,0,'Payroll can be paid electronically.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.A',3,'A vendor file stores information about:','["Owners", "Suppliers the business buys from", "Employees", "Customers"]'::jsonb,1,'It lists vendors.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.A',4,'A vendor file usually includes the vendor''s name, address, and:','["Birthday", "Hobby", "Payment terms", "Pet"]'::jsonb,2,'Terms drive payments.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.B',3,'A purchase on account increases:','["Revenue", "Accounts receivable", "Cash", "Accounts payable"]'::jsonb,3,'Buying on credit creates a payable.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.B',4,'Terms of 2/10, n/30 mean a 2% discount if paid within:','["10 days", "2 days", "20 days", "30 days"]'::jsonb,0,'2% discount within 10 days.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.C',3,'The accounts payable subsidiary ledger has an account for each:','["Customer", "Vendor", "Employee", "Owner"]'::jsonb,1,'It tracks each supplier.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.C',4,'The total of the subsidiary ledger should equal the:','["Revenue account", "Cash account", "Accounts payable control account", "Equity account"]'::jsonb,2,'Subsidiary ledger totals agree with control accounts.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.D',3,'Before paying an invoice, a clerk should compare it to the:','["Calendar", "Menu", "Poster", "Purchase order and receiving report"]'::jsonb,3,'A three-way match prevents errors.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.D',4,'An invoice for 100 units arrives but only 90 were received. The clerk should:','["Resolve the difference before paying", "Tear it up", "Pay anyway", "Ignore"]'::jsonb,0,'Pay for what was received.','original'),
