('127.256.d.6.E',4,'The schedule total of accounts payable should match the:','["Payroll total", "Inventory count", "Control account balance in the general ledger", "Bank balance"]'::jsonb,2,'They must agree.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.F',3,'Accounts payable appears on the balance sheet as a:','["Equity", "Asset", "Revenue", "Current liability"]'::jsonb,3,'It is owed within a year.','original'),
('127.256.d.6.F',4,'Paying down accounts payable reduces cash and also:','["Reduces liabilities", "Increases equity", "Increases assets", "Increases revenue"]'::jsonb,0,'Paying settles a debt.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.A',3,'Accounts receivable represents money:','["The business owes suppliers", "Customers owe the business", "Banks hold", "The owner invested"]'::jsonb,1,'Receivables are customer debts.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.A',4,'Accounts receivable is classified on the balance sheet as a:','["Expense", "Liability", "Current asset", "Equity"]'::jsonb,2,'It will be collected soon.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.B',3,'A customer file stores a customer''s name, address, and:','["Hobby", "Mascot", "Pet", "Credit terms"]'::jsonb,3,'Terms guide collection.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.B',4,'A customer file helps the business:','["Track and collect what customers owe", "Order paint", "Pay taxes", "Hire workers"]'::jsonb,0,'It supports billing.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.C',3,'A sale on account increases:','["Assets and liabilities only", "Accounts receivable and sales revenue", "Cash and expenses", "Payable and equity"]'::jsonb,1,'Credit sales create a receivable.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.C',4,'A $400 sale on account is recorded by debiting Accounts Receivable and crediting:','["Accounts Payable", "Cash", "Sales", "Supplies"]'::jsonb,2,'Revenue is credited.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.D',3,'The accounts receivable subsidiary ledger has an account for each:','["Owner", "Employee", "Vendor", "Customer"]'::jsonb,3,'It tracks each customer''s balance.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.D',4,'When a customer pays on account, the customer''s subsidiary balance:','["Decreases", "Doubles", "Increases", "Disappears"]'::jsonb,0,'Payments reduce balances.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.E',3,'A sales return occurs when a customer:','["Buys more", "Sends back merchandise for credit", "Opens an account", "Pays early"]'::jsonb,1,'Returns reduce sales.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.E',4,'A sales allowance is a reduction in price given because the goods were:','["Heavy", "Popular", "Damaged or not as ordered", "New"]'::jsonb,2,'Allowances compensate for defects.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.F',3,'When a customer sends a payment on account, the business debits Cash and credits:','["Inventory", "Sales", "Supplies", "Accounts Receivable"]'::jsonb,3,'The receivable is reduced.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.F',4,'A customer who pays within a discount period takes advantage of:','["A sales discount", "Penalty", "Interest", "Overdue fee"]'::jsonb,0,'Discounts encourage early payment.','original'),
('127.256.d.7.G',3,'An uncollectible account is a receivable the business:','["Owes", "Does not expect to collect", "Collected early", "Wrote in error"]'::jsonb,1,'Bad debt.','original'),
