('127.256.d.8.C',3,'Under FIFO, the first items purchased are assumed to be:','["Kept forever", "Sold first", "Sold last", "Returned"]'::jsonb,1,'First in, first out.','original'),
('127.256.d.8.C',4,'A store buys 10 units at $5, then 10 at $6. It sells 12 under FIFO. Cost of goods sold is:','["$72", "$66", "$62", "$60"]'::jsonb,2,'10 x 5 + 2 x 6 = 62.','original'),
('127.256.d.8.D',3,'When prices are rising, FIFO usually results in ending inventory that is:','["The same as LIFO", "Zero", "Lower than LIFO", "Higher in value than LIFO"]'::jsonb,3,'FIFO leaves the latest, higher costs in inventory.','original'),
('127.256.d.8.D',4,'When prices are rising, LIFO generally produces:','["Lower net income than FIFO", "Equal net income", "Higher net income", "No net income"]'::jsonb,0,'LIFO expenses the higher costs first.','original'),
